{"title":"Career Roadmap · Estimation Engineer","role":"Estimation Engineer","summary":"An Estimation Engineer prepares and analyses the expected cost, quantity, labour, material and equipment requirements for construction projects. The role connects quantity take-off, rate analysis, BOQ preparation, tendering, cost estimation, contracts and project planning.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build civil-engineering, quantity surveying, costing and construction-documentation fundamentals"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Develop expertise in estimation, tendering, quantity surveying or cost control"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Progress toward senior estimation, commercial management, contracts or cost-management roles"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Combine estimating with BIM, digital quantity take-off, data analytics, automation and construction technology"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Civil Engineering → Estimation Engineer","text":"Direct alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"Civil Engineering provides the foundation in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Construction materials"},{"text":"Building construction"},{"text":"Structural engineering"},{"text":"Surveying"},{"text":"Quantity estimation"},{"text":"Construction methods"},{"text":"Project management"},{"text":"Costing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should additionally develop quantity take-off, BOQ, rate analysis, tendering, billing, contracts, Excel, AutoCAD, BIM and estimation software."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Long-range horizons are planning guidance; exact industry requirements should be verified."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","bloc